Package: minisforum-n5-it5571-dkms
Version: @DEBVER@
Architecture: all
Maintainer: SirRenix <7069603+SirRenix@users.noreply.github.com>
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Depends: dkms (>= 3.0), proxmox-default-headers | linux-headers-amd64
Recommends: proxmox-default-headers
Section: kernel
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://github.com/SirRenix/minisforum-n5pro-fan-proxmox
Description: IT5571 EC fan driver for the Minisforum N5 Pro (DKMS)
 The out-of-tree hwmon driver ltdstudio/minisforum-n5-it5571 (upstream
 @TAG@, commit @COMMIT@) with the downstream patch series listed in
 /usr/src/minisforum-n5-it5571-<version>/PATCHES, as a DKMS module, rebuilt
 for every kernel whose headers are installed. On Proxmox VE the
 recommended proxmox-default-headers follows the default kernel series
 like proxmox-default-kernel does (proxmox-headers-<series> alone
 satisfies the dependency but stops at its series).
 .
 Enables the PWM nodes of the experimental N5 Pro profile
 (experimental_write=1 in /usr/lib/modprobe.d/) and loads the module at
 every boot (/usr/lib/modules-load.d/). Loading writes nothing to the EC;
 only a regulator such as n5-fangov writes.
 .
 Write gate: PWM writes only with DMI sys_vendor "Micro Computer (HK) Tech
 Limited" on the N5 PRO/F8NAA board (experimental_write=1) or the
 upstream-validated N5/F8NAA. The N5 Air and any system loaded with
 force=1 are read-only; read-only still sends EC read commands for the
 sensors.
 .
 Risk: with writes enabled a write goes straight to the fan output.
 0 stops a fan; the driver has no lower limit, no temperature check and no
 watchdog. The N5 Pro profile is experimental upstream and verified on one
 host only (N5 PRO/F8NAA, BIOS 1.05, EC 0.14). Handing a channel back to EC
 automatic restores regulation on the CPU channel; HDD regulation after the
 hand-back is not shown. The PCIe channel has no EC automatic: hand-back
 (pwm4_enable=2, unbind, unload) sets it to full speed. On reboot and
 power-off the driver sets the HDD and PCIe channels it touched to full
 speed and CPU/SSD to EC automatic. For read-only operation put
 "options minisforum_n5_it5571 experimental_write=0" into
 /etc/modprobe.d/minisforum-n5-it5571.conf. Details: README.md.
